acts_changed":[],"artifacts_created":[],"artifacts_deleted":[],"findings":[{"severity":"info","message":"Use exact paths: `rr.log(\"spear\", rr.ViewCoordinates.RIGHT_HAND_Z_UP, static=True)` for the Rerun world; `rr.log(\"spear/camera\", rr.Transform3D(translation=location_rr, mat3x3=R_rr_from_camera_rdf))`; `rr.log(\"spear/camera\", rr.Pinhole(..., camera_xyz=rr.ViewCoordinates.RDF, image_plane_distance=0.1, color=[255,128,0], line_width=0.003))`; then `rr.log(\"spear/camera/rgb\", rr.Image(...))`, `rr.log(\"spear/camera/depth_meters\", rr.DepthImage(..., meter=1.0))`, and optional modal streams such as `spear/camera/world_normal_visualization` and `spear/camera/diffuse_color`."},{"severity":"info","message":"`ViewCoordinates.RDF` is the right camera coordinate convention for the current matrix intent: X=right, Y=down, Z=forward. In Rerun 0.32, the preferred way is to set `camera_xyz=rr.ViewCoordinates.RDF` on the `Pinhole`; a static `rr.log(\"spear/camera\", rr.ViewCoordinates.RDF, static=True)` is also consistent but not necessary if `camera_xyz` is present. Do not use `RUB` unless the camera matrix is changed to columns `[right, up, back]`."},{"severity":"info","message":"`Transform3D` default relation maps from the entity space to its parent. For a camera pose under `spear/camera`, that is exactly camera-to-world. `mat3x3` should be a row-major 3x3 matrix whose columns are the child frame basis vectors expressed in the parent frame; Rerun applies the 3x3 first, then translation, so a camera point `p_cam` lands at `p_world = R @ p_cam + t`."},{"severity":"warning","message":"Rerun only supports right-handed coordinate systems. Raw Unreal/SPEAR world semantics are X=forward, Y=right, Z=up, which is not the same semantic basis as `RIGHT_HAND_Z_UP` (X=right, Y=forward, Z=up). The robust implementation is to convert all positions/vectors from Unreal to Rerun Z-up world before logging: `M_rr_from_ue = [[0,1,0],[1,0,0],[0,0,1]]`; `location_rr = M_rr_from_ue @ location_ue`; `R_rr_from_camera_rdf = M_rr_from_ue @ np.column_stack([right_ue, down_ue, forward_ue])`. This makes the camera RDF transform a proper right-handed pose in Rerun."},{"severity":"info","message":"The existing `get_unreal_rotation_matrix` basis is directionally correct for Unreal rotators: it produces columns `[forward_ue, right_ue, up_ue]` where zero rotation maps to +X, +Y, +Z and positive pitch aims +X toward +Z. The current `get_rerun_camera_matrix` correctly builds `[right_ue, down_ue, forward_ue]` for an RDF camera, but should be multiplied by the Unreal-to-Rerun world conversion if the root is logged as `RIGHT_HAND_Z_UP`."},{"severity":"high","message":"Current depth is logged at `spear/images/depth_meters`, outside the camera path. That prevents Rerun from associating the `DepthImage` with the camera pinhole for 3D backprojection and makes the point cloud/frustum origin wrong or disconnected. Move depth, RGB, and any image-plane modalities under `spear/camera/...`."},{"severity":"warning","message":"RGB channel handling should be explicit. Existing SPEAR examples often treat `final_tone_curve_hdr_` readback as BGRA/BGR and convert to RGB. For Rerun, either convert to RGB and use `rr.Image(rgb, color_model=\"RGB\")`, or pass the raw data with `color_model=\"BGR\"`/`\"BGRA\"` if shape and channels match. Avoid relying on shape-only inference when debugging color issues."},{"severity":"warning","message":"`diffuse_color` is not camera RGB; it is a material/albedo-like linear float modality. The current `to_rerun_albedo_image` clips linear values directly to uint8, which can look dark or odd. Prefer naming it `diffuse_color` rather than generic `albedo`, and for visualization use `np.power(np.clip(diffuse[:,:,:3], 0, 1), 1/2.2)` before converting to uint8. Existing Hypersim-oriented code treats diffuse channels `[0,1,2]` as RGB, so do not apply the final-tone-curve BGRA swap to diffuse unless live validation proves that specific buffer is BGR."},{"severity":